     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The maximum labeled dose is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in the US. Some references allow up to 3,000 mg/day. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg per administration. At this dose, the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity is substantial, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- **850 mg PO twice daily with meals** (1,700 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg total daily**, divided differently\n- Another dose\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, please confirm. I'll enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed the above-maximum dose. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
